# 10. NOTIFICATION SYSTEM

Use MongoDB to persist in-app notifications.

Supported events should include:
- Complaint submitted
- Complaint categorized
- Complaint assigned or reassigned
- Complaint status changed
- Complaint escalated
- Complaint resolved or reopened
- Feedback requested
- Important campus announcements

Each notification should include:
- Recipient
- Event type
- Title and message
- Related complaint ID, where applicable
- Created timestamp
- Read/unread state
- Relevant navigation target

### Notification reliability

- Create notifications through shared backend services.
- Use event identifiers or idempotency keys to prevent duplicates.
- Ensure that notifications are created only for authorized recipients.
- Use indexes for recipient and unread queries.
- Support pagination and mark-as-read actions.
- Make notification actions open the relevant complaint.
- Avoid blocking complaint submission when a non-critical email service is unavailable.

### Email and SMS

Email notifications should be supported through server-side configuration.

SMS can be optional and enabled only when configured.

If a notification provider fails:
- Record the failure safely.
- Retry transient failures with bounded backoff.
- Avoid duplicate messages.
- Provide an administrative view of delivery failures where appropriate.

Do not falsely report that an email or SMS was sent when the system only logged a dry-run message.

